  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689706",
      "title": "Managing Store Subscriptions",
      "lectureOrder": 105,
      "videoOrder": 93,
      "sourceHash": "06cbb794a034541e4943cddd4d2dc7b24162f39c1412592a8013d1617940b751",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.2,
          "end": 7.48,
          "en": "Now, the way I'm using the store thus far is good, but not ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.51,
          "end": 13.72,
          "en": "I'm setting up a subscription here, and in this application here, that is actually not a huge problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 13.72,
          "end": 18.94,
          "en": "because in this application, the component where I create the subscription, so the card component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 18.97,
          "end": 21.43,
          "en": "is always added to the Dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 21.76,
          "end": 24.28,
          "en": "Now let's assume this is not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 24.31,
          "end": 28.15,
          "en": "Let us say we have a button here in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 31.68,
          "en": "So let's quickly import it from the folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 33.69,
          "end": 34.95,
          "en": "And this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 36.67,
          "end": 39.37,
          "en": "Should manage whether we see the card or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 39.96,
          "end": 44.49,
          "en": "So we can add a variable show cart and set this equal to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 45.34,
          "end": 45.94,
          "en": "Or to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.94,
          "end": 46.36,
          "en": "Initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.36,
          "end": 47.08,
          "en": "Maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.23,
          "end": 48.91,
          "en": "And then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.55,
          "end": 54.95,
          "en": "Here at the bottom or maybe above the card doesn't really matter too much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.98,
          "end": 60.17,
          "en": "I'll add a button where I say toggle cart and upon click on this button here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.99,
          "end": 63.81,
          "en": "I want to set show card.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.7,
          "end": 65.99,
          "en": "To what it's currently not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.99,
          "end": 67,
          "en": "So I invert it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.01,
          "end": 68.66,
          "en": "If it's true, I set it to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.66,
          "end": 70.52,
          "en": "If it's false, I set it to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.21000000000001,
          "end": 74.36,
          "en": "The card should then be only shown if show card is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.51,
          "end": 78.41,
          "en": "So we can use if here show card and close the if block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.41,
          "end": 79.97,
          "en": "Now why am I doing this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 84.06,
          "en": "If I do that button is not placed in a nice way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.06,
          "end": 87.21000000000001,
          "en": "But that doesn't matter if I do that and I add something to the cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.36,
          "end": 88.07,
          "en": "Toggle the cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.08,
          "end": 88.88,
          "en": "It's gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 89.98,
          "en": "It's there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90,
          "end": 91.68,
          "en": "I can do this as often as I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.71000000000001,
          "end": 98.1,
          "en": "Now, what we don't see here is that we actually introduced a quite significant bug in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.1,
          "end": 100.47,
          "en": "And do you have an idea what the bug could be?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.92,
          "end": 104.05,
          "en": "It's related to our subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.2,
          "end": 110.05,
          "en": "Whenever this component gets added, remember that this whole script section here executes and that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.05,
          "end": 111.72999999999999,
          "en": "means we set up a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.94,
          "end": 116.91,
          "en": "When we remove the component from the Dom, however, this subscription is not cleared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.92,
          "end": 122.74,
          "en": "So in memory, in our ongoing JavaScript application, which of course does not finish just because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.74,
          "end": 128.14,
          "en": "we detach that in memory, this subscription is still ongoing and whenever we add something to the cart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.17,
          "end": 133.93,
          "en": "this now actually triggers all ongoing subscriptions, even the subscriptions of the components which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.93,
          "end": 136.21,
          "en": "aren't even attached to the Dom anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.24,
          "end": 139.78,
          "en": "Everything has been disposed, but this subscription hasn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.96,
          "end": 142.66,
          "en": "So you should always clean up your subscriptions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.66,
          "end": 143.71,
          "en": "And how can you do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.71,
          "end": 148.27,
          "en": "How can you clean up that subscription when a component is unmounted, when it is removed?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.43,
          "end": 155.16,
          "en": "Well, the good thing is the subscribe function here actually returns something which you can store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.16,
          "end": 158.45,
          "en": "in a constant, and that something is a function itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.46,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "It's an unsubscribe function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 165.48,
          "en": "Now, of course, you don't have to name the constant unsubscribe, but that is what the function which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.48,
          "end": 167.04,
          "en": "subscribe returns will do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.04,
          "end": 169.02,
          "en": "It will clear this subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.11,
          "end": 170.76,
          "en": "And now to clear the subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.76,
          "end": 175.8,
          "en": "Whenever this component is removed, we can simply import ondestroy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.38,
          "end": 183.14,
          "en": "The life cycle hook you learn about earlier in the course from Svelte because you learned that this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.17,
          "end": 186.47,
          "en": "allows you to run code when the component gets removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.59,
          "end": 194.54,
          "en": "So here we can then add ondestroy and inside of that function which we pass to Ondestroy, we can check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 194.54,
          "end": 196.59,
          "en": "if unsubscribe exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.61,
          "end": 199.79,
          "en": "It normally should always exist, but nonetheless.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.82,
          "end": 203.57,
          "en": "And if it does, we simply call unsubscribe like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 203.75,
          "end": 206.36,
          "en": "Now the behavior here is the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 206.36,
          "end": 214.28,
          "en": "We can still toggle that how often we want, but we also now always clear the subscription when we remove",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 214.28,
          "end": 216.23,
          "en": "the component which created it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 216.23,
          "end": 218.78,
          "en": "And every new component receives its own subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.78,
          "end": 223.91,
          "en": "But the old subscriptions are not going on in the background and that avoids memory leaks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 223.91,
          "end": 226.76,
          "en": "So you should always clear your subscriptions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 226.76,
          "end": 230.57,
          "en": "That is really important to keep in mind and to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
